fted harmonics**: Take the quad-frequency approach from curve_2_v7.py but add phase offsets: `np.sin(2 * np.pi * freq * t + phi)` where phi = \u03c0/4 for secondary frequencies\n\n**Mandatory constraints for all 5 curves:**\n- Keep `num_lines = 300` (proven optimal)\n- Keep total perturbation amplitudes below 0.025 combined\n- Use only prime frequencies between 11-53\n- Maintain the base serpentine structure with alternating line directions\n\nGenerate these 5 curves and report back the results."
